  "description": "DUNMIK crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4 2 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H120 Cu8 Dy4 N16 O40. From the CIF bond table, Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1A (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1B (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1C (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu1D (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu1F (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1E (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1G (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu1E (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.227-3.871 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.42-110.25°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C96H112Cu8Dy4N16O40. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
